              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-31802\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: tar\nFixed Version: 7.5.11\nLink: [CVE-2026-31802](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31802)\nnode-tar is a full-featured Tar for Node.js. Prior to version 7.5.11, tar (npm) can be tricked into creating a symlink that points outside the extraction directory by using a drive-relative symlink target such as C:../../../target.txt, which enables file overwrite outside cwd during normal tar.x() extraction. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.5.11.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-31802**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|tar|7.5.11|[CVE-2026-31802](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-31802)|\n\nnode-tar is a full-featured Tar for Node.js. Prior to version 7.5.11, tar (npm) can be tricked into creating a symlink that points outside the extraction directory by using a drive-relative symlink target such as C:../../../target.txt, which enables file overwrite outside cwd during normal tar.x() extraction. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.5.11."
